      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Electricity"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Electric current is the rate of flow of electric charge through a conductor.",
        "Voltage (Potential Difference) provides the electrical energy required to push current through a circuit.",
        "Ohm's Law states that current is directly proportional to voltage and inversely proportional to resistance (V = IR).",
        "Magnets exert forces via magnetic fields, and electromagnets create controllable magnetic fields using electric current."
      ],
      "id": "kgkx7if"
